-T 1C
# Scalpel (affected-module detection) is disabled by default; no Maven
# invocation builds with it unless -Dscalpel.enabled=true is passed. The only
# consumer is the scalpel-report CI job in verify.yaml, which runs mode=report
# (analysis only, no reactor changes). mode is pinned here too so an ad-hoc
# -Dscalpel.enabled=true never trims the reactor or skips tests by surprise.
-Dscalpel.enabled=false
-Dscalpel.mode=report
# disableTriggers: changes to CI/build config disable Scalpel entirely (full build).
-Dscalpel.disableTriggers=.github/**,.mvn/**,mvnw*
# excludePaths: non-build files ignored in change detection (add new non-Maven dirs here).
# Every root after ui/** is named by no pom in the reactor, so a change under it
# cannot affect any module. Listing it stops a commit that touches it from being
# attributed to the root aggregator and projecting a full 57-module build.
# Weigh the cost before adding an entry: a commit confined to an excluded root
# exhausts the filters, and with buildAllIfNoChanges=true pinned below that
# builds every module, so a genuine build input wrongly listed here degrades to
# a full build rather than passing silently. The residual cost of a wrong entry
# is on mixed commits, where the excluded file is invisible to attribution. The
# full version history behind that is in .github/workflows/README.md, "Reading
# the Scalpel report". That is why the list stays short and every absence below
# is argued rather than assumed.
# No slash-free pattern is used, and that is deliberate: Scalpel rewrites a
# pattern containing no slash to also match at any depth, so *.md would hide
# the 111 tracked markdown files inside module trees, including test fixtures
# such as app/src/test/resources/git/invalid-content-ref/README.md that
# GitOpsStatusTest loads. Scalpel 0.3.10 compiled slash-free patterns against
# the root only, so the 0.4.x pin silently widened them; the probe evidence is
# recorded in .github/workflows/README.md, "Reading the Scalpel report".
# Root-level markdown and LICENSE are left unlisted on purpose: no pom names a
# root file, so a change confined to one projects the zero-build-set report,
# which under the buildAllIfNoChanges pin below builds every module. adr/ is
# tracked markdown and listed explicitly; claudedocs/ is gitignored and its
# stray .txt/.zip/.html are untracked, so no diff ever reports them.
# docs/** predates this list and is its one entry naming a reactor module,
# apicurio-registry-docs. A change confined to docs/ therefore projects no build
# of that module. Pre-existing behaviour, left alone here rather than widened.
# Four roots are deliberately absent. .checkstyle/ is a real build input, named
# by the configLocation that the root pom sets and every module inherits.
# .github/ and .mvn/ are disable triggers above, which is the stronger
# treatment. scripts/ holds validate-files.sh, which CI runs as a gate.
# console-plugin/ is absent for its own reason: its frontend files still project
# a full build, while its backend Java module (a full-profile module, absent
# from this job's reactor and already invisible to the pom-boundary rule) would
# be blinded for any future scalpel-enabled -Dfull run by a wholesale exclusion.
-Dscalpel.excludePaths=docs/**,ui/**,typescript-sdk/**,python-sdk/**,docs-playbook/**,adr/**,.claude/**,.opencode/**,branding/**,ide-config/**,.githooks/**
# buildAllIfNoChanges: when Scalpel finds nothing to build, either because every
# changed file matched excludePaths or because the diff is empty, handing Maven
# a zero-project reactor fails the build outright with NoGoalSpecifiedException:
# a session with no projects has no goals (REG-304, reproduced on this pin in
# both mode=trim and mode=skip-tests). true routes both cases to a full build.
# Nothing is lost by never building zero modules: a build with no goals
# verified nothing anyway, and the commits whose pipeline can be skipped
# outright are already handled by the path filters in the decide job.
-Dscalpel.buildAllIfNoChanges=true
# failSafe: on any Scalpel error, fall back to a full build instead of failing
-Dscalpel.failSafe=true
